      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine how many minutes it will take for the printer to print 200 pages given that it prints 17 pages per minute. We can use the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{\\text{Total Pages}}{\\text{Pages per Minute}}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{200 \\text{ pages}}{17 \\text{ pages per minute}}\n\\]\n\nWe will now calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# given values\ntotal_pages = 200\npages_per_minute = 17\n\n# calculating time in minutes\ntime_minutes = total_pages / pages_per_minute\n# rounding to the nearest whole number\ntime_minutes_rounded = round(time_minutes)\n\nprint(time_minutes_rounded)\n```\n```output\n12\n```\nThe time it will take for the printer to print 200 pages is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) minutes.",
